---
description: Multi-tenant data isolation
alwaysApply: true
---

Single database, shared schema, 11 clinics, one operator.

Every domain table carries a non-null `clinic_id` foreign key.

All data access goes through a repository layer in `src/server/repo/`. Those
functions take `clinicId` as an explicit first argument. Never call the Drizzle
client directly from a route handler, server action, or worker job.

There is no cross-clinic read anywhere in the product. If a query would need
one, that is a bug in the requirement, not a reason to widen the scope.

The audit log records `clinic_id`, actor, action, before and after. Every
approve, edit, reject, send, and knowledge base change is logged.
